      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name may come from the Allegewi tribe that once lived along the Allegheny River or from a Native word meaning \"beautiful.\"",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allegany%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Allegany was first settled around 1820 by Ebenezer Reed, a Connecticut native, before becoming the Town of Burton in 1831.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allegany%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Allegany Area Historical Association, founded during the village’s 1981 sesquicentennial, preserves and shares the region’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
